WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.944
[MUSIC]

00:00:06.944 --> 00:00:09.840
We fully commit to that event.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:12.630
The story is very much about
how do heroes move forward

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.130
from that kind of a loss.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.079
It's a unique
circumstance because I

00:00:16.079 --> 00:00:18.940
don't know that there was
ever a movie of that scale

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.480
and that budget where
the lead character is

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:22.663
lost at the end of the film.

00:00:22.663 --> 00:00:23.830
And that's what we focus on.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:25.920
We focus on surprising
ourselves, surprising

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.808
the audience, making
really dramatic choices

00:00:28.808 --> 00:00:31.350
that we're not sure how we're
going to get out of as artists.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.580
Killing half the
characters, and then

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.970
trying to figure out how
you move forward from there.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:39.250
That is a compelling
place to put yourself in.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:40.340
We don't chase bigger.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.320
What we do chase is
great storytelling.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.390
[MUSIC]

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:46.765
Whenever you're
working with IMAX

00:00:46.765 --> 00:00:48.310
you're thinking about scale.

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:49.810
You're thinking
about top to bottom,

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:51.160
as well as side to side.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:54.330
[MUSIC]

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:56.730
For movies like this
with cosmic settings

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:00.480
and larger than life characters,
there's no better way

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.160
to shoot it, and
there's no better way

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.160
to display it for an audience.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:09.870
The epic scale of these movies
requires a canvas like that.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:14.850
Even if there's a small
chance, we owe this to everyone

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:17.670
who is not in this room to try.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:19.620
Whatever it takes.

00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:20.910
Whatever it takes.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:22.250
Whatever it takes.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:24.740
You're dealing with a lot
of really unique voices, who

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:26.510
have a lot to say,
and are moving

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:29.000
in different tones, and
different directions,

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.230
making really different
choices from one another.

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:32.100
And that's exciting.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.890
We're so close to
all of them now.

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:34.730
It's like family.

00:01:34.730 --> 00:01:37.340
Robert would always host
lunch for everyone, every day,

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.330
and that's probably
my fondest memories.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:42.790
It really was like summer
camp for all of us.

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:43.750
I like this one.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:46.840
We have to expend a
lot of energy and time

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.540
making sure we keep
the information

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:51.820
about the movie really
controlled, and focused,

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:52.490
and quiet.

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:55.810
Because the pleasure that we
get from experiencing movies

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:57.550
for the first time
in the theater,

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:59.140
and not having
anything tipped, it's

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:00.910
just like we want
other audiences

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:03.480
to have that opportunity.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:06.750
Everyone has great TVs and
sound systems at home now.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:09.000
Why are they going to come
out and sit in the theater?

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.490
Well, you're going to give
them the grandest experience

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:12.760
that they can possibly have.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.424
[MUSIC]

00:02:15.424 --> 00:02:17.770
We think that people
who go see it in IMAX

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.920
are going to be blown away.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:31.808
[MUSIC]

